  "title": "Irrationality criteria for Lambert subseries",
  "subject": "Erdős #257",
  "subject_kind": "problem",
  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 26,
  "question": "Which supports are proved to give irrational Lambert subseries, and what still blocks the arbitrary infinite support that Erdős #257 asks about?",
  "precis": "The series ∑_{a∈A}(b^a−1)^{-1} is irrational for every integer b≥2 and infinite A contained in E∪V when E satisfies a finite-prime weighted summability condition and V has a summable positive divisor cover. The two classes are incomparable, and their union reaches supports in neither class. A common average over dyadic lengths produces one index with both displacements small. Arbitrary infinite supports at base two remain unresolved.",
  "owns": "the weighted, divisor-cover and mixed support criteria with complete proofs and method limits; the long paper treats finite denominators, the achievement set and rational membership",
  "not_authority_for": "the validity of claims tagged Lean, which belongs to the cited kernel-checked source, or a solution to Erdős #257, which remains open",
